        dcterms:description """In classical geometry, the "Radial Distance" is a coordinate in polar coordinate systems (r, $\\theta$).
    Basically the radial distance is the scalar Euclidean distance between a point and the origin of the system of coordinates.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
