            "Micromol pe Metru Pătrat Secundă"@ro,
            "Micromol na Kvadratni Meter Sekunda"@sl,
            "Micromol per Metrekare Saniye"@tr ;
        dcterms:description """One part per 10**6 (million) of the SI unit of quantity of matter (the mole) per SI unit area per SI unit
    of time.  This term is based on the number of photons in a certain waveband incident per unit time (s) on a unit area (m2)
    divided by the Avogadro constant (6.022 x 1023 mol-1). It is used commonly to describe PAR in the 400-700 nm waveband.
    Definition Source: Thimijan, Richard W., and Royal D. Heins. 1982. Photometric, Radiometric, and Quantum Light Units of
    Measure: A Review of Procedures for Interconversion. HortScience 18:818-822.
  """@en ;
        qudt:applicableSystem sou:SI ;
        qudt:conversionMultiplier 0.000001 ;
        qudt:conversionMultiplierSN 1e-06 ;
        qudt:hasDimensionVector qkdv:A1E0L-2I0M0H0T-1D0 ;
        qudt:hasFactorUnit _:ne65d4cbea54444c6960902e3884365fdb3155,
            _:ne65d4cbea54444c6960902e3884365fdb3156,
            _:ne65d4cbea54444c6960902e3884365fdb3157 ;
        qudt:hasQuantityKind quantitykind:PhotosyntheticPhotonFluxDensity ;
        qudt:symbol "μmol/(m²·s)"^^xsd:string ;
        qudt:ucumCode "umol.m-2.s-1"^^qudt:UCUMcs ;
        qudt:unitForQuantityKind quantitykind:PhotosyntheticPhotonFluxDensity ;
        rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/3.4.0/vocab/unit> .

