        qudt:isoNormativeReference "http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=43012"^^xsd:anyURI ;
        qudt:latexDefinition "$r = \\overrightarrow{OP}$, where $O$ and $P$ are two points in space."^^qudt:LatexString ;
        qudt:plainTextDescription """A "Position Vector", also known as location vector or radius vector, is a Euclidean vector which
    represents the position of a point P in space in relation to an arbitrary reference origin O.
