            "Normkubikmeter"@de,
            "Normal Cubic Metre"@en,
            "Normal Cubic Meter"@en-us ;
        dcterms:description """The $\\textit{normal cubic metre}$ is a unit representing the amount of a product contained in a volume
    of one cubic metre at reference 'normal' temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of the actual amount of
    product, most commonly referring to oil, not the volume of the product. The reference conditions for normal cubic metre vary
    depending on purpose and application.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
        qudt:conversionMultiplier 0.0 ;
        qudt:conversionMultiplierSN 0e+00 ;
