        dcterms:description """The picocurie (pCi) is $10^{-12}$ of the curie, a non-SI unit of radioactivity. $1\\,\\text{pCi} = 3.7
    \\times 10^{-2}\\,\\text{Bq} = 0.037$ radioactive disintegrations per second. It is commonly used in environmental monitoring,
    particularly for radon activity in air and water.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
