        dcterms:description """Joule Per Kelvin (J/K) is a unit in the category of Entropy. It is also known as joules per kelvin,
    joule/kelvin. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Joule Per Kelvin (J/K) has a dimension of $ML^{2}T^{-2}Q^{-1}$
