            "立体角度"@zh ;
        dcterms:description """The solid angle subtended by a surface S is defined as the surface area of a unit sphere covered by the
    surface S's projection onto the sphere. A solid angle is related to the surface of a sphere in the same way an ordinary angle
    is related to the circumference of a circle. Since the total surface area of the unit sphere is 4*pi, the measure of solid
    angle will always be between 0 and 4*pi.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
        qudt:applicableUnit unit:DEG2,
            unit:FA,
            unit:SR ;
        qudt:dbpediaMatch "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Solid_angle"^^xsd:anyURI ;
