        qudt:plainTextDescription """The solid angle subtended by a surface S is defined as the surface area of a unit sphere covered by
    the surface S's projection onto the sphere. A solid angle is related to the surface of a sphere in the same way an ordinary
    angle is related to the circumference of a circle. Since the total surface area of the unit sphere is 4*pi, the measure of
    solid angle will always be between 0 and 4*pi.
  """^^xsd:string ;
        qudt:qkdvDenominator qkdv:A0E0L2I0M0H0T0D0 ;
