        rdfs:label "Standard Gravitational Parameter"@en ;
        dcterms:description """In celestial mechanics the standard gravitational parameter of a celestial body is the product of the
    gravitational constant G and the mass M of the body. Expressed as $\\mu = G \\cdot M$. The SI units of the standard
    gravitational parameter are $m^{3}s^{-2}$.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
