    coulomb/square metre. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Coulomb Per Square Meter (C/m2) has a dimension of
    $L^{-2}TI$ where $L$ is length, $T$ is time, and $I$ is electric current. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.
  """^^qudt:LatexString ;
