        qudt:latexDefinition "$n = \\frac{N}{V}$, where $N$ is the number of particles and $V$ is volume."^^qudt:LatexString ;
        qudt:plainTextDescription """In physics, astronomy, and chemistry, number density (symbol: n) is a kind of quantity used to
    describe the degree of concentration of countable objects (atoms, molecules, dust particles, galaxies, etc.) in the
