        qudt:plainTextDescription """Energy per unit area is a measure of the energy either impinging upon or generated from a given
    unit of area. This can be a measure of the "toughness" of a material, being the amount of energy that needs to be applied per
    unit area of a crack to cause it to fracture. This is a constant for a given material..
  """^^xsd:string ;
